### Search MQL custom object records (insert-only cursor pattern)
POST https://api.hubapi.com/crm/v3/objects/2-61391055/search
Authorization: Bearer {{HUBSPOT_API_KEY}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "filterGroups": [
    {
      "filters": [
        { "propertyName": "hs_object_id", "operator": "GT", "value": "0" }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "properties": ["mql_reason", "mql_date", "email", "contact_sales_message", "hubspot_owner_id"],
  "sorts": [{ "propertyName": "hs_object_id", "direction": "ASCENDING" }],
  "limit": 200
}

### Enumerate PQL custom object properties (includeHidden matters)
GET https://api.hubapi.com/crm/v3/properties/2-63308387?archived=false&includeHidden=true
Authorization: Bearer {{HUBSPOT_API_KEY}}

### Batch read MQL -> contact associations (v4, max 100 inputs)
POST https://api.hubapi.com/crm/v4/associations/2-61391055/contacts/batch/read
Authorization: Bearer {{HUBSPOT_API_KEY}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "inputs": [
    { "id": "60076957267" }
  ]
}

### Batch read contacts by id (missing ids are silently omitted)
POST https://api.hubapi.com/crm/v3/objects/contacts/batch/read
Authorization: Bearer {{HUBSPOT_API_KEY}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "inputs": [{ "id": "501" }],
  "properties": ["firstname", "lastname", "email", "lifecyclestage", "lead_accepted", "lead_disqualification_reason", "sla_violation", "sla_violation_date", "hubspot_owner_id"]
}
